9	 * when present, otherwise country code '+61' is assumed and a single leading '0' is dropped from
10	 * the national digits. Spaces, dashes and brackets are stripped, and 8 to 15 digits are required
11	 * after the '+'. The national-number length must also match the country code ('+61' requires 9
